@startuml dispatch-seam
' ============================================================================
' agentd platform — the DISPATCH SEAM (2026-07-18). ONE Tool.execute() written
' by the author; the engine picks the executor by provenance + runtime. Same
' code on desktop and web because keys and paths were always behind a seam.
' Two blocks: (1) the seam, (2) who-does-what for a sandboxed model-using call.
' PUML only; do not render PNG unless asked.
' ============================================================================
title The dispatch seam — one execute(), two executors

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 17
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #888888
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

rectangle "Tool author writes ONE\nasync execute(params) -> ToolResult\n(no keys; writes to workspace; declares artifacts)" as TOOL #F5F0FF

rectangle "agentd dispatch\ndecides by PROVENANCE (built-in vs user-authored)\n+ RUNTIME (desktop vs web)" as DISP

package "LOCAL executor  (desktop, and trusted built-ins on web)" as LOC #F0FFF0 {
  rectangle "run in-process / local subprocess\nfs = whole machine (desktop) or user root (web)\nmodel seam -> user's key (BYOK) OR gateway" as LE
}

package "SANDBOX executor  (web: custom plugins, exec, heavy)" as SBX #FFF0F0 {
  rectangle "dispatch to a per-run sandbox\nfs = mounted user dir ONLY\nmodel seam -> gateway VIRTUAL KEY" as SE
}

TOOL --> DISP
DISP --> LE : trusted / local
DISP --> SE : untrusted / web

note bottom of DISP
  The tool NEVER changes. Two conventions that already hold in agentd make this work:
  (1) tools get their model through the seam (resolve_tool_model -> litellm), never a raw key;
  (2) tools write to current_workspace(), never a fixed path. So swapping the credential and
  the mount BEHIND the seam is invisible to the tool. Desktop today already IS the local executor.
end note
@enduml


@startuml sandbox-call-sequence
title Who does what — a sandboxed, model-using tool call (web)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 16
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #888888
  ParticipantBackgroundColor White
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

participant "Agent loop +\nSandbox Executor\n(agentd core)" as E
participant "Model Proxy\n(our LiteLLM svc)" as G
participant "Orchestrator\n(ECS/Fargate ctl)" as O
participant "Runner\n(inside the sandbox)" as R
database "User dir\n/users/uid (EFS)" as D
participant "LLM provider" as P

E -> E : agent calls tool T\nprovenance = user-authored -> sandbox path
E -> G : mint VIRTUAL KEY\n(user_id, run_id, allowed models, budget, ~min TTL)
G --> E : virtual key
E -> O : start runner: mount EFS access point (/users/uid/agents/id),\nzero-perm IAM, net policy, cpu/mem/time caps,\ninject gateway_url + virtual key, pass params
O -> R : launch microVM (Firecracker)
activate R
R -> D : load plugin from mounted plugins/
R -> R : await execute(params)  (the SAME code as desktop)
R -> G : model call with virtual key
G -> P : forward with OUR real provider key
P --> G : completion
G -> G : meter usage -> RDS
G --> R : completion
R -> D : write durable output to workspace/
R --> E : ToolResult + artifact refs
deactivate R
E -> O : kill task
E -> G : revoke virtual key
E -> E : resume loop with the result

note over E, P
  DESKTOP path = the LOCAL executor: steps to the Gateway/Orchestrator vanish
  (model call uses the user's own key or the gateway directly; execute() runs
  in-process on their machine). The execute() body is byte-for-byte identical.
end note
@enduml
